WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.407
The voice is the first thing viewers judge in a narrated video.

2
00:00:04.457 --> 00:00:08.844
Here's how to choose a narrator voice and speed that let your content do the talking.

3
00:00:09.344 --> 00:00:11.755
Don't judge a voice on its sample sentence.

4
00:00:11.805 --> 00:00:16.782
Paste in a real paragraph with the hard bits: names, numbers, acronyms.

5
00:00:16.832 --> 00:00:19.860
Compare two or three, then pick the easiest to follow.

6
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.795
Speed matters as much as the voice.

7
00:00:22.845 --> 00:00:26.823
Too slow feels patronising, too fast loses people.

8
00:00:26.873 --> 00:00:31.284
If captions flick past, slow down; if you want to skip, speed up.

9
00:00:31.784 --> 00:00:34.787
A synthetic narrator reads exactly what you write.

10
00:00:34.837 --> 00:00:36.250
So 'Q3 rev.

11
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.896
up 8%' becomes 'Revenue in the third quarter rose eight per cent.'

12
00:00:41.396 --> 00:00:44.864
Each slide stays up as long as its narration lasts.

13
00:00:44.914 --> 00:00:50.532
For quiet slides or silent loops, set a minimum time per slide so nothing flashes past.

14
00:00:51.032 --> 00:00:55.974
On Pro, a.i. directs the video, timing each animated scene to your narration.

15
00:00:56.024 --> 00:01:00.167
Try Basic first, then hear your deck at powerpoint2vid.com.

